  "notes": "SD Guthrie Berhad (Bursa Malaysia: 5285) \u2014 world's largest oil-palm planter by certified-sustainable hectarage, ~568,000 ha (~1,400K acres) across Malaysia, Indonesia, Papua New Guinea/Solomon Islands, and Liberia. Formerly Sime Darby Plantation Berhad \u2014 carved out of Sime Darby Berhad's three-way demerger and listed on Bursa Malaysia Main Market on 30 November 2017; rebranded SD Guthrie Berhad in late 2024 to reclaim the historical 'Guthrie' identity that traces back to the 1821 founding of Guthrie & Co. Reportable IFRS 8 segments: Upstream Malaysia (FFB, CPO, PK), Upstream Indonesia, Upstream PNG/Solomons (legacy New Britain Palm Oil consolidated 2018), Downstream (refineries, oleochemicals, biofuels \u2014 Europe + Asia footprint), and Other (R&D, agribusiness services). Calendar fiscal year (Dec 31). Quarterly figures from Bursa Malaysia Form 8 reports filed via the IR portal; annual aggregates from Sime Darby Plantation / SD Guthrie annual reports' 5-year financial highlight tables. RM-billion figures translated to MYR-million (\u00d7 1000). Acres derived from disclosed planted hectares \u00d7 2.47 \u00f7 1000. Net debt = total borrowings \u2212 cash & cash equivalents. NAV/share = total equity attributable to owners / weighted shares outstanding (~6,915M). Major events captured: 2017 demerger + Bursa listing; 2018 New Britain Palm Oil full consolidation; 2021-22 CPO super-cycle (price spike to RM7,000+/MT on Russia/Ukraine sunflower oil disruption); 2020-2024 US Customs and Border Protection Withhold Release Order over forced-labor allegations (issued Sep 2020, modified Jan 2024 allowing US imports to resume); late-2024 SD Guthrie rebrand. Some quarterly EBITDA values are estimates triangulated from disclosed quarterly PBT + finance costs + D&A where the quarterly Form 8 did not break out segment EBITDA explicitly. Pre-FY2017 not included \u2014 Sime Darby Plantation only became a stand-alone listed entity from 30 Nov 2017, so older figures are embedded inside legacy Sime Darby Berhad consolidated accounts and not directly comparable.",
